  "id": "method-of-loci",
  "term": "method of loci",
  "definition": "The method of loci is a memory strategy that uses imagined familiar places to help encode and later recall information. A person mentally places items in selected locations within a remembered environment and then retrieves them by mentally moving through that “memory palace.”",
